# Task 145-003 Execution Plan — EventBus Abstraction + Subscribe API

## Overview
Create an in-process event bus (EventBus) that wraps Node.js EventEmitter, providing:
- publish/subscribe with sprintId + channel filtering
- tail() for reading last N events from JSONL
- watchFile() for cross-process event detection
- Integration into existing writeEvent() in event-stream.ts

## Files to Create
1. `src/orchestra/event-bus.ts` (~200 LoC) — EventBus class + singleton export

## Files to Modify
2. `src/orchestra/event-stream.ts` — Add eventBus.publish(event) after JSONL write in writeEvent()

## Files to Create (Tests)
3. `tests/orchestra/event-bus.test.ts` — 10+ tests covering all spec requirements

## Implementation Details

### EventBus class
- Extends EventEmitter
- `publish(event)` → emits 'event' with DeckentEvent payload
- `subscribe(sprintId, channels, fn)` → listener with sprintId + channel filter, returns unsubscribe fn
- `tail(sprintId, n)` → reads JSONL file, returns last N parsed events
- `watchFile(sprintId)` → fs.watch on JSONL, parse new lines, publish
- `unwatchAll()` → close all FSWatcher instances

### event-stream.ts integration
- Import eventBus singleton
- After appendFileSync in writeEvent(), call eventBus.publish(event) in try/catch
- Publish error must NOT block file write (fail-safe)

### Type alignment
- Task spec says EventMessage/Channel but actual codebase uses DeckentEvent/ChannelCode
- Will use DeckentEvent and ChannelCode (actual types) for compatibility

## Test Plan (8+ tests)
1. publish → subscribe direct delivery
2. subscribe channels filter (NOTIFY only → PHASE skipped)
3. subscribe sprintId filter (sprint-144 sub → sprint-145 event ignored)
4. unsubscribe stops delivery
5. publish error → handler exception swallowed
6. tail() last 5 lines parsed correctly
7. tail() empty/missing file → []
8. writeEvent integration → eventBus.publish called
9. unwatchAll cleans up watchers
10. multiple subscribers receive same event

## Risks
- fs.watch behavior varies by platform (Linux inotify OK for CI)
- watchFile test needs real file I/O (use tmp dir)
